<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Sapienza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1209">1209</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Sapienza was an agreement of 1209 between the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geoffrey-i-of-villehardouin">Geoffrey I of Villehardouin</a>, ruler of the Frankish Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>. Named after the island of Sapienza off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/methoni">Modon</a>, it recognised Venetian possession of the ports of Modon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koroni">Coron</a>, while Geoffrey acknowledged Venetian overlordship for his principality and granted Venetians trading privileges.</p></div>
